<h2>7. Dual-Tier Fallback Resiliency Pipeline</h2>
<p>To operate at 100% service uptime during api key resets, corporate sandbox testing, or API quota outages, implement this complete dual-tier fallback router in your backend service code:</p>

<pre>
import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";

// 1. Quota &amp; Rate Error Sieve
export function isQuotaOrApiKeyError(err: any): boolean {
  if (!err) return false;
  const msg = (err.message || String(err)).toLowerCase();
  return (
    msg.includes("429") ||
    msg.includes("resource_exhausted") ||
    msg.includes("quota") ||
    msg.includes("api key") ||
    msg.includes("limit") ||
    msg.includes("unauthorized") ||
    msg.includes("fetch") ||
    msg.includes("cors")
  );
}

// 2. Multi-tier High-Availability Router
export async function executeProspectResearch(companyInput: string, geminiKey?: string): Promise&lt;any&gt; {
  // Tier 0: Gemini API
  if (geminiKey) {
    try {
      const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: geminiKey });
      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({
        model: "gemini-2.5-flash",
        contents: `Conduct analytical discovery on target company/domain: "${companyInput}"`,
        // Include search tools for grounding
        config: {
          tools: [{ googleSearch: {} }],
          responseMimeType: "application/json"
        }
      });
      return JSON.parse(response.text);
    } catch (err) {
      if (isQuotaOrApiKeyError(err)) {
        console.warn("[Router] Tier 0 Exhausted. Re-routing stream to Tier 1 NVIDIA NIM...");
      } else {
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }

  // Tier 1: NVIDIA Llama3 NIM Cloud Node Fallback
  if (process.env.NVIDIA_API_KEY) {
    try {
      const nvResponse = await fetch("https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions", {
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
          "Content-Type": "application/json",
          "Authorization": `Bearer ${process.env.NVIDIA_API_KEY}`
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          model: "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct",
          messages: [
            { role: "system", content: "You are an elite enterprise B2B consultant..." },
            { role: "user", content: `Analyze domain/company "${companyInput}"` }
          ],
          temperature: 0.15,
          response_format: { type: "json_object" }
        })
      });
      if (nvResponse.ok) {
        const payload = await nvResponse.json();
        return JSON.parse(payload.choices[0].message.content);
      }
    } catch (nvError) {
      console.error("[Router] Tier 1 NVIDIA NIM Failed:", nvError);
    }
  }

  // Tier 2: Fully Local Sandbox Estimation Fallback Engine
  console.warn("[Router] Falling back to Tier 2 local-logic heuristics");
  return generateLocalResearchFallback(companyInput);
}
</pre>

<h2>8. Copywriting Standards & Channel Budget Boundaries</h2>
<p>To avoid delivery blocking, bounce rate climbs, or frame layouts shearing, the output generator operates under strict length block metrics:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>WhatsApp Target Notes:</strong> <code>&lt; 100 Words</code>. Zero hyperlinks. Includes a warm personal observation followed by an operational process offer.</li>
  <li><strong>LinkedIn Invite Text:</strong> <code>&lt; 40 Words</code>. Networking focus. Hard selling and pitch comments are strictly prohibited.</li>
  <li><strong>LinkedIn Main Sequence Message:</strong> <code>&lt; 80 Words</code>. Shares specific performance metrics for lookalike enterprise competitors.</li>
  <li><strong>Cold Email Subject Lines:</strong> <code>&lt; 7 Words</code>. Casual, lowercase, conversational patterns (e.g., <i>"quick question about [topic]"</i>).</li>
  <li><strong>Main Cold Email Copy:</strong> <code>120 - 150 Words</code>. Built on the 4-part value block architecture:
    <ol>
      <li>Relatable personalized opener citing crawled profile facts.</li>
      <li>Identified corporate challenge based on technological detection.</li>
      <li>Concrete proof point establishing solutions efficiency.</li>
      <li>Low-friction call to action (Low-friction request to coordinate calendar space).</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Email Sequence Followup:</strong> <code>&lt; 60 Words</code>. Single-question challenge reminder.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Database Normalization & Serialization Schema</h2>
<p>To track team research and share lists smoothly, outcomes are serialized directly into a cloud repository (such as Firestore) using this template structure:</p>

<pre>
Collection Name: prospect_researches
Document Path: /prospect_researches/{documentId}

Document Structure:
{
  "id": "String (Auto-generated Unique Identifier)",
  "companyName": "String (Target Corporate Entity)",
  "domain": "String (Target Internet Destination Suffix)",
  "createdAt": "Timestamp (ISO 8601 or Cloud Registry Timestamp)",
  "reportJSON": "String (Serialized payload mapping to ProspectResearchReport interface)",
  "userId": "String (Authoring Identity coordinates)",
  "orgId": "String (Sharing Group Tenant coordinates)"
}
</pre>

